                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "<p>The nurse is preparing to teach ostomy care to a client who has just had a urinary diversion; the client expresses concern about body appearance. Which client action indicates that the best initial positive adaptation is being made?</p>",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "a0f7d178f7b728b8bba7ef20ddeca62d",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Evaluating 评价",
                        "textAnalysis": "<p>Rationale:</p><p>The best initial positive step in learning to care for an ostomy and to accept it as a part of the self is to be able to look at the ostomy. Once the client is able to look at the ostomy and touch it, the client can proceed more successfully to learn about ostomy care. The other options all indicate a deferral or refusal on the part of the client, which makes them less than optimal choices.</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(30, 30, 30);\">Test-Taking Strategy:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(30, 30, 30);\">Note the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 129, 208);\">strategic words,</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(30, 30, 30);\">&nbsp;</span><em style=\"color: rgb(30, 30, 30);\">best initial</em><span style=\"color: rgb(30, 30, 30);\">. Eliminate options 2, 3, and 4 because they are&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 129, 208);\">comparable or alike.</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(30, 30, 30);\">&nbsp;Options 3 and 4 do not illustrate adaptation in any way and are eliminated first. The correct option is an action on the part of the client, whereas option 2 is still a refusal to participate in any way in ostomy care.</span></p>",
                        "id": "2f076cd968a1434289975833a284cb49",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "bc2467a0929d4d38a5b7d5ee9fd00415",
                                "content": "Presence of hand railings in the bathroom"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "9340af19155145c69b72fe08f2a46c92",
                                "content": "Having one bathroom on each floor of the home"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "348d11f877294cdd83180d92580719e7",
                                "content": "Bathroom located on the second floor, bedroom on the first floor"
