                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is assessing a client who has been experiencing leakage of small amounts of urine throughout the day and night. The client reports a history of uterine prolapse. The nurse performs a physical assessment and notes a distention in the suprapubic area. Based on the history and assessment, the nurse would suspect which type of incontinence?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nOverflow incontinence occurs when pressure of urine in bladder overpowers bladder sphincter control, resulting in leakage of small amounts of urine throughout the day and night. The client may also void small amounts of urine, and the bladder is usually distended and palpable. Potential causes of overflow incontinence include conditions that result in bladder or urethral outlet obstruction, such as bladder neck obstruction, urethral stricture, underactive detrusor muscle, or pelvic organ prolapse, which increases the pressure on the bladder. The client's experience of small amounts of urine leakage throughout the day and night, the history of uterine prolapse, and the distended and palpable bladder support the diagnosis of overflow incontinence. Therefore, option 3 is correct. Urge incontinence can be due to an overactive bladder and can be caused by physical problems such as damage to the spine, brain, or the nerves between the spine and the bladder. Stress incontinence occurs when a strain is placed on the bladder, as when the client coughs and sneezes; it may be due to weak pelvic floor muscles. Functional incontinence occurs when other diseases or disabilities such as arthritis or dementia make it difficult for the client to get to the bathroom and undressed in time.",
                        "id": "3e172678649d436db2361e63a9bbe67f",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
