                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is caring for a client diagnosed with a ureteral stricture with complicated hydronephrosis. The client had a ureteral stent placed. The client’s last blood urea nitrogen (BUN) level was 28 mg/dL (10.1 mmol/L). Which laboratory value indicates a therapeutic response to the treatment plan?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nA ureteral stricture results in narrowing of the ureter, which can occur along any point of the ureter. Ureteral strictures usually form due to adhesions or scar tissue related to surgery or radiation, but they can be congenital in nature. Hydroureter and hydronephrosis can result if urine is unable to pass through the stricture, causing ureteral and renal dilation and kidney damage. A blood urea nitrogen (BUN) level is 10-20 mg/dL (3.6-7.1 mmol/L). Therefore, all of the presented options indicate elevated BUN levels. However, compared to the client’s last BUN level, options 2, 3, and 4 are all higher in comparison, indicating a worsening in renal function. While option 1 is still considered an elevated BUN level, it is trending downward and indicates a therapeutic response to the treatment plan. Therefore, option 1 is correct.",
                        "id": "4178ee845b734cd68af286da4881accc",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "316c9ce2ccdc4673978968987eccea56",
                                "content": "It may be due to an increase in serotonin levels."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "af2dee32e6a3456d8d0aa3664ef431e1",
                                "content": "It may be due to overhydration with intravenous fluids."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "f10ea263458c4d6ca992374e0a8d5818",
                                "content": "It may be due to the client's hemoglobin of 13.2 g/dL (132 mmol/L)."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "1dd95a505639404e879a0547018e92e4",
                                "content": "It may be a consequence of decreased dopaminergic receptor stimulation."
                            }
                        ],
